        <headline>Small Craft Advisory issued September 24 at 8:22PM AKDT until September 25 at 5:00PM AKDT by NWS Juneau AK</headline>
        <description>Southeast Alaska Coastal Waters from Dixon Entrance to
Cape Suckling out 100 NM

Wind forecasts reflect the predominant speed and direction
expected. Seas forecasts represent the average of the highest
one-third of the combined windwave and swell height.

UPDATED

...SMALL CRAFT ADVISORY FRIDAY...

.REST OF TONIGHT...E wind 20 kt. Seas 7 ft.
.FRI...SE wind 25 kt. Seas 7 ft.
.FRI NIGHT...SE wind 25 kt. Seas 10 ft. Showers late.
.SAT...SE gale to 35 kt. Seas 11 ft. Showers.
.SAT NIGHT...SE wind 25 kt. Seas 12 ft. Showers.
.SUN...S wind 25 kt. Seas 12 ft.
.MON...SE wind 15 kt. Seas 9 ft.
.TUE...S wind 15 kt. Seas 6 ft.
</description>
